WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.237 --> 00:00:01.886
- Discipline is your best friend.

00:00:01.886 --> 00:00:04.950
It will take care of you
like nothing else can.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.367
Do not take the easy way out.

00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:11.599
Do not give up based on instinct.

00:00:12.551 --> 00:00:13.718
Take the step.

00:00:15.746 --> 00:00:18.663
Step aggressively toward your fear.

00:00:20.558 --> 00:00:22.567
- He's an American podcaster, author

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.980
and retired United States Navy SEAL.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.139
He received the silver
star and the bronze star

00:00:27.139 --> 00:00:29.413
for his actions in the Iraq war.

00:00:29.413 --> 00:00:31.896
He started a weekly podcast
covering topics like leadership,

00:00:31.896 --> 00:00:35.587
exercise and lessons
from a former Navy SEAL.

00:00:35.587 --> 00:00:38.027
He's Jocko Willink, and
here's my take on his top 10

00:00:38.027 --> 00:00:39.295
rules for success.

00:00:39.295 --> 00:00:41.388
Rule number six is my personal favorite

00:00:41.388 --> 00:00:43.567
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.429
Also guys, as you're watching,
if you hear something

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:46.584
that really resonates with you,

00:00:46.584 --> 00:00:48.309
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:50.030
put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:50.931
by your sharing.

00:00:50.931 --> 00:00:52.865
And also when you write it down,

00:00:52.865 --> 00:00:55.871
you're much more likely to
lock it in for yourself too.

00:00:55.871 --> 00:00:57.042
Enjoy.

00:00:57.042 --> 00:00:59.909
(whooshing)

00:00:59.909 --> 00:01:02.492
(upbeat music)

00:01:09.871 --> 00:01:12.410
- One of my direct
subordinates, one of my guys

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.900
that worked for me, he would call me up

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.209
or pull me aside with some major problem,

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.347
some issue that was going on.

00:01:19.347 --> 00:01:21.943
And he'd say Boss, we got this
and that and the other thing.

00:01:21.943 --> 00:01:25.354
And I'd look at him and I'd say, "Good."

00:01:25.354 --> 00:01:28.359
And finally one day he was
telling me about some issue

00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:30.881
that he was having, some problem

00:01:30.881 --> 00:01:33.873
and he said, I already know
what you're going to say.

00:01:33.873 --> 00:01:35.254
And I said, well what am I going to say?

00:01:35.254 --> 00:01:37.837
He said, you're going to say good.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.688
He said, that's what you always say.

00:01:40.688 --> 00:01:43.488
When something is wrong and going bad,

00:01:43.488 --> 00:01:47.113
you always just look at me and say good.

00:01:47.113 --> 00:01:49.170
And I said, well, yeah.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:53.337
When things are going bad,
there's going to be some good

00:01:54.672 --> 00:01:56.585
that's going to come from it.

00:01:56.585 --> 00:01:59.855
Didn't get the new high
speed gear we wanted?

00:01:59.855 --> 00:02:01.317
Good.

00:02:01.317 --> 00:02:03.751
Didn't get promoted.

00:02:03.751 --> 00:02:05.220
Good.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.862
More time to get better.

00:02:06.862 --> 00:02:08.724
Oh, mission got canceled?

00:02:08.724 --> 00:02:10.315
Good, we can focus on another one.

00:02:10.315 --> 00:02:11.766
Didn't get funded.

00:02:11.766 --> 00:02:14.154
Didn't get the job you wanted.

00:02:14.154 --> 00:02:17.612
Got injured, sprained my
ankle, got tapped out?

00:02:17.612 --> 00:02:18.550
Good

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.739
Got beat?

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.192
Good.

00:02:21.192 --> 00:02:22.192
You learned.

00:02:24.456 --> 00:02:26.623
Unexpected problems, good.

00:02:27.479 --> 00:02:31.562
We have the opportunity
to figure out a solution.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.035
That's it.

00:02:34.035 --> 00:02:37.836
When things are going bad,
don't get all bummed out,

00:02:37.836 --> 00:02:41.253
don't get startled, don't get frustrated.

00:02:44.238 --> 00:02:47.655
If you can say the word good, guess what?

00:02:50.112 --> 00:02:52.720
It means you're still alive.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.608
It means you're still breathing.

00:02:54.608 --> 00:02:57.025
And if you're still breathing

00:02:58.191 --> 00:02:59.703
or in hell,

00:02:59.703 --> 00:03:02.691
you've still got some fight left in you.

00:03:02.691 --> 00:03:04.358
So get up, dust off,

00:03:06.274 --> 00:03:07.107
reload,

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.223
recalibrate, reengage.

00:03:14.213 --> 00:03:16.296
And go out on the attack.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:22.757
I always say that discipline
is the root of all good

00:03:22.757 --> 00:03:23.590
qualities.

00:03:25.937 --> 00:03:29.687
But you have to absolutely
apply it to things

00:03:30.811 --> 00:03:33.353
outside of just waking up early.

00:03:33.353 --> 00:03:36.004
It's everything, it's
working out every day.

00:03:36.004 --> 00:03:40.159
Making yourself stronger
and faster and more flexible

00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:41.326
and healthier.

00:03:43.301 --> 00:03:47.468
Discipline is eating the right
foods to fuel your system.

00:03:51.438 --> 00:03:54.521
It's about disciplining your emotions

00:03:55.646 --> 00:03:56.909
so you can make good decisions.

00:03:56.909 --> 00:04:01.076
It's about having the
discipline to control your ego

00:04:02.838 --> 00:04:07.005
so your ego doesn't get out
of hand and control you.

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:12.329
It's about treating people the way you

00:04:12.329 --> 00:04:14.246
would want to be treated.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:20.572
And doing the tasks that you
don't necessarily want to do,

00:04:20.572 --> 00:04:22.904
but that you know will help you.

00:04:22.904 --> 00:04:24.404
Or help your team.

00:04:26.795 --> 00:04:29.212
It's about facing your fears.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:34.330
Takes discipline to face your fears

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.330
so you can conquer them.

00:04:40.388 --> 00:04:42.207
And that's what discipline is.

00:04:42.207 --> 00:04:44.088
Discipline means taking the hard road.

00:04:44.088 --> 00:04:47.490
The uphill road to do what's right

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.323
for yourself and for other people.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.633
It's so often the easy path,

00:05:00.411 --> 00:05:04.875
the easy path that calls to
us to be weak for that moment,

00:05:04.875 --> 00:05:07.375
to break down for that moment.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.577
To give in to the desire and
the short term gratification.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:19.710
But the discipline will not allow that.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.726
The discipline calls for
strength and fortitude

00:05:23.726 --> 00:05:24.559
and will.

00:05:26.954 --> 00:05:28.760
It won't accept weakness.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.843
It won't tolerate another break down.

00:05:35.235 --> 00:05:37.152
The discipline can seem

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.730
like it's your worst enemy,

00:05:44.416 --> 00:05:45.916
but the reality is

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:50.273
discipline is your best friend.

00:05:50.273 --> 00:05:53.879
It will take care of you
like nothing else can.

00:05:53.879 --> 00:05:56.379
And it'll put you on that path

00:05:58.587 --> 00:06:03.061
the path to strength and
health and intelligence

00:06:03.061 --> 00:06:04.228
and happiness.

00:06:08.348 --> 00:06:12.348
And most importantly,
it'll put you on that path

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.710
to freedom.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.864
People want to know how
to stop the laziness,

00:06:19.864 --> 00:06:23.222
and they want to know how
to stop the procrastination.

00:06:23.222 --> 00:06:27.241
And you know, they have
some idea in their head,

00:06:27.241 --> 00:06:31.408
you know, some kind of a
vision of what they want to do.

00:06:35.124 --> 00:06:36.460
But they don't know where to start.

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:37.775
They don't know where
to start it, ya know?

00:06:37.775 --> 00:06:40.753
They don't know where to start.

00:06:40.753 --> 00:06:44.160
And so they say, hey, where do I start?

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.094
And when's the best time to start?

00:06:46.094 --> 00:06:49.511
And I have a very simple answer for that.

00:06:50.621 --> 00:06:51.704
Here and now.

00:06:55.628 --> 00:06:56.661
That's it.

00:06:56.661 --> 00:06:58.584
You want to improve?

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.119
You want to get better?

00:07:01.119 --> 00:07:02.819
You want to get on a workout program

00:07:02.819 --> 00:07:04.525
or a clean diet?

00:07:04.525 --> 00:07:06.775
You want to start a business?

00:07:08.448 --> 00:07:11.491
You want to write a book or
make a movie or build a house,

00:07:11.491 --> 00:07:15.658
or a computer or put together
some mobile application?

00:07:18.379 --> 00:07:19.962
Where do you start?

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:23.776
You start right here.

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:24.875
And when do you start?

00:07:24.875 --> 00:07:26.542
You start right now.

00:07:28.199 --> 00:07:31.622
You initiate the action aggressively.

00:07:31.622 --> 00:07:32.455
Ya go.

00:07:34.646 --> 00:07:38.263
'Cause the idea isn't
going to execute itself.

00:07:38.263 --> 00:07:40.274
And the book isn't going to write itself.

00:07:40.274 --> 00:07:42.051
And the weights out in the gym,

00:07:42.051 --> 00:07:44.024
they're not going to move themselves.

00:07:44.024 --> 00:07:47.774
You have to do it, and
you have to do it now.

00:07:49.763 --> 00:07:53.499
And that means you got to
stop thinking about it,

00:07:53.499 --> 00:07:55.578
and stop dreaming about it

00:07:55.578 --> 00:07:58.347
and stop researching every aspect of it

00:07:58.347 --> 00:08:00.667
and reading all about
it, and debating the pros

00:08:00.667 --> 00:08:01.885
and cons of it.

00:08:01.885 --> 00:08:03.552
Just start doing it.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.870
Take that first step.

00:08:10.764 --> 00:08:12.347
And make it happen.

00:08:13.187 --> 00:08:14.824
Get after it.

00:08:14.824 --> 00:08:16.991
Get after it here and now.

00:08:19.723 --> 00:08:24.595
Person's strengths are often
their biggest weaknesses.

00:08:24.595 --> 00:08:28.972
And so that also means
that their weaknesses

00:08:28.972 --> 00:08:30.889
can be their strengths.

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:34.478
So, me?

00:08:38.188 --> 00:08:39.021
I am weak.

00:08:39.965 --> 00:08:42.210
In all those ways that I listed.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:43.043
I am weak.

00:08:46.681 --> 00:08:48.979
But I don't accept that.

00:08:48.979 --> 00:08:51.190
I don't accept that I am what I am,

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:54.440
and that that is what I'm doomed to be.

00:08:57.183 --> 00:08:59.407
No, I don't accept that.

00:08:59.407 --> 00:09:00.490
I'm fighting.

00:09:02.017 --> 00:09:03.406
I'm always fighting.

00:09:03.406 --> 00:09:06.996
I'm struggling and I'm
scrapping and I'm kicking

00:09:06.996 --> 00:09:09.944
and I'm clawing at those weaknesses.

00:09:09.944 --> 00:09:12.111
To change them, stop them.

00:09:15.624 --> 00:09:16.957
Some days I win.

00:09:19.407 --> 00:09:20.907
Some days I don't.

00:09:22.377 --> 00:09:25.877
But each and every day, I get back up

00:09:25.877 --> 00:09:27.460
and I move forward,

00:09:29.427 --> 00:09:31.835
with my fist clenched

00:09:31.835 --> 00:09:35.085
toward the battle, toward the struggle.

00:09:36.782 --> 00:09:39.315
And I fight with everything
I've got to overcome those

00:09:39.315 --> 00:09:43.232
weaknesses and those
shortfalls and those flaws

00:09:44.754 --> 00:09:48.754
as I strive to be just a
little bit better today

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.592
than I was yesterday.

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:55.821
First of all, before the
war, the military sent me

00:09:55.821 --> 00:09:56.654
to college.

00:09:56.654 --> 00:09:57.736
So I had to go to college.

00:09:57.736 --> 00:10:01.163
And as I said before, I was
super focused when I went

00:10:01.163 --> 00:10:02.080
to college.

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:05.027
I'd been in the SEAL teams for 10 years.

00:10:05.027 --> 00:10:07.243
I was a go-getter, I was a hard charger.

00:10:07.243 --> 00:10:08.510
I was like oh, you want
me to read this book?

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:12.107
Boom, I would sit down and
just force myself to read it.

00:10:12.107 --> 00:10:14.904
And then got back to the SEAL teams

00:10:14.904 --> 00:10:17.544
and like when I went to college,

00:10:17.544 --> 00:10:21.196
I literally read every single
thing that I was assigned.

00:10:21.196 --> 00:10:24.335
And nobody does that in
college, nobody does that.

00:10:24.335 --> 00:10:27.256
I read every single page
of every single thing I was

00:10:27.256 --> 00:10:28.601
assigned during college.

00:10:28.601 --> 00:10:31.214
That's ridiculous, it's
almost a waste of time.

00:10:31.214 --> 00:10:32.729
It's almost embarrassing.

00:10:32.729 --> 00:10:35.157
Echo definitely thinks
it's a waste of time.

00:10:35.157 --> 00:10:38.762
But it was because I just could just

00:10:38.762 --> 00:10:40.559
lock my brain down and get it done.

00:10:40.559 --> 00:10:42.954
So then get back to the
teams and in the teams,

00:10:42.954 --> 00:10:44.812
officer in the teams you
have a lot of administrative

00:10:44.812 --> 00:10:47.688
paperwork to do, evaluations
and after actions reports

00:10:47.688 --> 00:10:48.902
and all these things.

00:10:48.902 --> 00:10:50.163
And I would do the same thing.

00:10:50.163 --> 00:10:51.761
I would just go on a lock
down mode and I would put

00:10:51.761 --> 00:10:53.681
my brain on it and boom
I'd go through it and just

00:10:53.681 --> 00:10:54.514
get it done.

00:10:54.514 --> 00:10:55.906
I would just be able to focus.

00:10:55.906 --> 00:10:57.405
- So like, each thing,

00:10:57.405 --> 00:10:59.264
- Laser focus, laser focus.

00:10:59.264 --> 00:11:02.729
- So that report, done, gone, memo, gone.

00:11:02.729 --> 00:11:03.943
Report, done.

00:11:03.943 --> 00:11:08.372
- There's another kind of
instinct that you need to be

00:11:08.372 --> 00:11:09.626
on the lookout for.

00:11:09.626 --> 00:11:11.209
This one is a liar.

00:11:12.277 --> 00:11:14.277
This one is a saboteur.

00:11:16.343 --> 00:11:18.426
This one is a back biter.

00:11:20.203 --> 00:11:24.286
And like the devil himself,
he's a shape shifter.

00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:29.741
He's going to disguise
himself and make you think

00:11:29.741 --> 00:11:32.741
he's got your best interest in mind.

00:11:35.222 --> 00:11:36.472
But he doesn't.

00:11:37.793 --> 00:11:41.876
This is the instinct that
says you've had enough.

00:11:43.517 --> 00:11:46.253
This is the instinct that
says you've given it your

00:11:46.253 --> 00:11:47.135
best shot.

00:11:47.135 --> 00:11:48.718
You can stand down.

00:11:50.332 --> 00:11:51.749
You can back off.

00:11:53.168 --> 00:11:54.835
You can take a knee.

00:11:57.370 --> 00:12:01.370
This is the instinct that
says you can rest now.

00:12:06.109 --> 00:12:08.594
Do not listen to that instinct.

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:09.761
Do not listen.

00:12:11.909 --> 00:12:16.076
That instinct is a liar and
wants to bring you down.

00:12:16.938 --> 00:12:21.587
That's the instinct that's
a defense mechanism.

00:12:21.587 --> 00:12:24.378
Wants to give you an out.

00:12:24.378 --> 00:12:28.840
A place to run to, a
little place of sympathy.

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:32.205
An amnesty, a little place of amnesty

00:12:32.205 --> 00:12:36.372
where everything's forgiven,
where all these failures

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:42.608
can gather together in comfort
and drown their sorrows

00:12:42.608 --> 00:12:44.691
in lies and in deception.

00:12:48.464 --> 00:12:50.464
And they tell each other

00:12:52.421 --> 00:12:56.504
and they'll tell you, you
did the best you could.

00:12:57.931 --> 00:13:02.098
They'll say the deck, the
deck was stacked against you.

00:13:03.363 --> 00:13:06.363
And they'll say it's not your fault.

00:13:09.436 --> 00:13:12.686
And they'll tell you it's okay to stop.

00:13:14.622 --> 00:13:16.390
It's okay to settle.

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:18.140
It's okay to give up.

00:13:23.191 --> 00:13:26.438
And that is the instinct to fight,

00:13:26.438 --> 00:13:30.271
ya need to push back to
smash into the ground.

00:13:31.336 --> 00:13:33.753
Do not take the easy way out.

00:13:35.803 --> 00:13:39.036
Do not give up based on instinct.

00:13:39.036 --> 00:13:42.703
If you are forced to
stand down, to retreat,

00:13:44.399 --> 00:13:48.399
so that you can rebuild
and re-attack, so be it.

00:13:51.801 --> 00:13:54.968
But make that decision based on logic.

00:13:57.671 --> 00:14:01.338
Not on the instinct of
surrender and defeat.

00:14:06.042 --> 00:14:09.042
And you need to train that instinct.

00:14:11.649 --> 00:14:13.368
Your instinct.

00:14:13.368 --> 00:14:15.285
Train it to say get up.

00:14:16.785 --> 00:14:17.868
Go, fight on.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:24.823
And if that is what you become,

00:14:25.744 --> 00:14:30.616
if that becomes your fundamental
reaction to adversity,

00:14:30.616 --> 00:14:33.449
if that becomes your gut instinct,

00:14:37.604 --> 00:14:42.221
then you will overcome just
about anything that stands

00:14:42.221 --> 00:14:43.929
in your path.

00:14:43.929 --> 00:14:45.846
There's been thousands,

00:14:48.137 --> 00:14:50.872
and hundreds of thousands,
millions of warriors

00:14:50.872 --> 00:14:53.539
that have been in very stressful

00:14:55.516 --> 00:14:59.287
situations and faced evil and faced death.

00:14:59.287 --> 00:15:01.704
Much worse than the situation

00:15:03.803 --> 00:15:05.563
I'm in or you're in

00:15:05.563 --> 00:15:08.189
that we might consider stressful.

00:15:08.189 --> 00:15:10.779
And I even did this when I was overseas,

00:15:10.779 --> 00:15:14.572
when I was on deployment,
when I was a combat leader.

00:15:14.572 --> 00:15:16.506
I was feeling stress.

00:15:16.506 --> 00:15:19.397
And you know what, we took
casualties and it was awful,

00:15:19.397 --> 00:15:21.897
and it was heart breaking and,

00:15:25.753 --> 00:15:27.420
But there were other

00:15:29.778 --> 00:15:32.035
soldiers and warriors throughout time

00:15:32.035 --> 00:15:35.699
that have been in much worse situations.

00:15:35.699 --> 00:15:39.866
Gettysburg or Vicksburg or
the Battle of the Bulge.

00:15:41.424 --> 00:15:44.507
And in all those horrible situations,

00:15:47.591 --> 00:15:51.758
they proved, really that
humans can withstand almost

00:15:52.846 --> 00:15:55.096
almost unimaginable stress.

00:15:57.319 --> 00:16:00.935
Which meant to me that I could too.

00:16:00.935 --> 00:16:01.935
And you can.

00:16:04.827 --> 00:16:07.339
And the first step for me, is doing that,

00:16:07.339 --> 00:16:10.756
taking that look to gain some perspective

00:16:13.415 --> 00:16:16.792
and then in order to gain
perspective you got to do

00:16:16.792 --> 00:16:18.045
something that we already talked about,

00:16:18.045 --> 00:16:21.919
you've got to detach, you've
got to detach from the problems

00:16:21.919 --> 00:16:25.627
or the stress that you're experiencing

00:16:25.627 --> 00:16:29.377
so that you can get that
perspective of them.

00:16:30.937 --> 00:16:31.770
Now,

00:16:33.902 --> 00:16:36.482
there's a couple
different types of stress.

00:16:36.482 --> 00:16:39.183
Now if it's something that
you can control that's

00:16:39.183 --> 00:16:41.456
causing you stress,

00:16:41.456 --> 00:16:45.155
well, why aren't you
getting control of it?

00:16:45.155 --> 00:16:47.570
Now there's also stress that's
caused by things that you

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.144
cannot control.

00:16:49.144 --> 00:16:53.311
And if you remember talking
earlier about artillery

00:16:54.266 --> 00:16:57.556
and how horrible that was,
and what made it so horrible

00:16:57.556 --> 00:17:01.229
was that there was no control over it.

00:17:01.229 --> 00:17:04.517
So if you can't control something

00:17:04.517 --> 00:17:07.184
and you can't get control of it,

00:17:08.414 --> 00:17:11.914
you have to at least embrace what you can.

00:17:13.247 --> 00:17:15.929
And I'm not saying you're going
to embrace artillery shelling,

00:17:15.929 --> 00:17:17.799
but I'll tell you what,

00:17:17.799 --> 00:17:20.861
when it comes to things like artillery

00:17:20.861 --> 00:17:24.108
or for us in Ramadi, was IEDs.

00:17:24.108 --> 00:17:26.715
And we could do everything
we could do to mitigate

00:17:26.715 --> 00:17:27.876
that risk,

00:17:27.876 --> 00:17:30.990
but eventually there's
only so much you can do,

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:34.181
and you cannot completely eliminate it.

00:17:34.181 --> 00:17:37.322
But you can't control it, so
why you going to worry about it?

00:17:37.322 --> 00:17:39.822
Why you going to stress about it?

00:17:41.197 --> 00:17:45.178
If there's something that's
completely beyond your control,

00:17:45.178 --> 00:17:47.020
you cannot, you've got to detach from it

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:51.211
and not let yourself
get stressed about it.

00:17:51.211 --> 00:17:52.794
And on top of that,

00:17:54.962 --> 00:17:56.544
if it's something that you can't control,

00:17:56.544 --> 00:17:58.575
how can you look at it
in a different light?

00:17:58.575 --> 00:18:01.202
How can see it in a way
that you could actually take

00:18:01.202 --> 00:18:02.535
advantage of it?

00:18:05.438 --> 00:18:06.771
How can you take

00:18:08.377 --> 00:18:11.404
that stress and make it
into some kind of ally.

00:18:11.404 --> 00:18:15.571
You know, the chaos of combat
is something that I couldn't

00:18:16.971 --> 00:18:19.445
control, but I had to
embrace it so I could try

00:18:19.445 --> 00:18:23.253
and figure out how I could
take advantage of it.

00:18:23.253 --> 00:18:25.503
So when it comes to stress,

00:18:26.825 --> 00:18:28.075
don't fight it.

00:18:30.186 --> 00:18:32.603
Turn it on itself and use it.

00:18:33.749 --> 00:18:34.604
Use it.

00:18:34.604 --> 00:18:38.054
Use it to make yourself
sharper and more alert.

00:18:38.054 --> 00:18:41.889
And use it to make yourself
think more and learn more

00:18:41.889 --> 00:18:43.885
and get better.

00:18:43.885 --> 00:18:45.468
And use that stress

00:18:47.392 --> 00:18:50.559
as a catalyst to make yourself better.

00:18:51.691 --> 00:18:55.059
- Your book isn't, I
mean, it's thick, but,

00:18:55.059 --> 00:18:57.195
I should have been able to
read this in two or three

00:18:57.195 --> 00:18:58.372
solid days of reading.

00:18:58.372 --> 00:18:59.205
- [Jocko] Yes.

00:18:59.205 --> 00:19:00.930
- I told you how successful I was.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:02.057
- [Jocko] Yes, not very.

00:19:02.057 --> 00:19:05.159
- And that bugs the shit out of me.

00:19:05.159 --> 00:19:07.742
(Jocko laughs)

00:19:09.933 --> 00:19:10.766
It's a fail.

00:19:10.766 --> 00:19:11.599
It's a,

00:19:13.118 --> 00:19:14.743
- You know what though, I think this is,

00:19:14.743 --> 00:19:16.331
- It's a failure on my part.

00:19:16.331 --> 00:19:18.526
- I think that this is
the same thing that we

00:19:18.526 --> 00:19:21.039
were talking about on the last podcast.

00:19:21.039 --> 00:19:25.106
And I think Echo said, when
you say aw, you know what,

00:19:25.106 --> 00:19:27.650
I'm not going to finish
this book right now,

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:28.859
I don't really want to.

00:19:28.859 --> 00:19:30.966
It's sort of like when you
say, oh I'm not going to--

00:19:30.966 --> 00:19:33.004
- No, it's not that I
didn't want to though.

00:19:33.004 --> 00:19:34.765
- That's what I'm saying, you
say, but I don't want to do it

00:19:34.765 --> 00:19:37.363
right now, I can push it off a little bit.

00:19:37.363 --> 00:19:40.696
You accept that, you accept that answer.

00:19:42.004 --> 00:19:43.695
You accept that answer.

00:19:43.695 --> 00:19:47.612
The soldier, Jody, wouldn't
accept that answer.

00:19:49.608 --> 00:19:50.441
Would not.

00:19:50.441 --> 00:19:52.057
- Do you self talk?

00:19:52.057 --> 00:19:54.140
- Not really, not really.

00:19:55.056 --> 00:19:56.809
I'm not a guy that says, you
know, I'm going to do this

00:19:56.809 --> 00:19:57.642
or I'm going to do that.

00:19:57.642 --> 00:19:58.725
I just do it.

00:19:59.919 --> 00:20:01.499
I just go and do whatever that thing is.

00:20:01.499 --> 00:20:05.930
You know I actually took
this question from Twitter

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:09.263
and I answered the question in one word.

00:20:12.251 --> 00:20:15.834
You've lived a life
dominated by doubt and fear,

00:20:15.834 --> 00:20:18.251
how do you step into bravery?

00:20:22.752 --> 00:20:23.585
Step.

00:20:26.013 --> 00:20:28.062
That's how you step into bravery.

00:20:28.062 --> 00:20:29.448
Step.

00:20:29.448 --> 00:20:30.615
Take the step.

00:20:32.831 --> 00:20:35.748
Step aggressively toward your fear.

00:20:37.942 --> 00:20:41.942
And that, that step toward
your fear is the step

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:44.053
into bravery.

00:20:46.884 --> 00:20:51.051
Because we're, we're scared
of what we don't know.

00:20:53.019 --> 00:20:55.102
And there is only one way

00:20:57.969 --> 00:20:59.636
to learn and to know

00:21:00.741 --> 00:21:02.947
and that is to confront that fear.

00:21:02.947 --> 00:21:05.591
You have to step, you have to go.

00:21:05.591 --> 00:21:07.508
And this simple action,

00:21:08.967 --> 00:21:10.717
this simple attitude,

00:21:12.096 --> 00:21:14.513
it answers so many questions.

00:21:16.285 --> 00:21:20.452
My theory here would be if
you're afraid of fighting,

00:21:21.709 --> 00:21:23.919
and altercations, go train ju jitsu,

00:21:23.919 --> 00:21:25.685
if you're afraid of heights,

00:21:25.685 --> 00:21:27.761
work on some rock climbing.

00:21:27.761 --> 00:21:31.564
If you're afraid of water, time
to swim, it's time to surf.

00:21:31.564 --> 00:21:32.944
It's time to get out there.

00:21:32.944 --> 00:21:35.312
If you're afraid of pull ups, do pull ups.

00:21:35.312 --> 00:21:37.330
If you're afraid of squats, do squats.

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:41.082
If you're afraid of public
speaking, go speak in public.

00:21:41.082 --> 00:21:42.200
- Mmhmm.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:46.308
- If yo're afraid to start a
business, start a business.

00:21:46.308 --> 00:21:47.309
Make it small.

00:21:47.309 --> 00:21:49.106
And on all these, what you
have to do is you have to

00:21:49.106 --> 00:21:52.453
mitigate the risk and you
have to ease yourself into it

00:21:52.453 --> 00:21:54.474
but you got to for it.

00:21:54.474 --> 00:21:58.057
And eventually you will
overcome that fear.

00:22:01.044 --> 00:22:04.942
But the hard part is you
got to take the first step.

00:22:04.942 --> 00:22:08.725
You got to take that first
step to begin to inoculate

00:22:08.725 --> 00:22:11.465
yourself against the fear.

00:22:11.465 --> 00:22:14.195
Against the fear of the
thing that's in your mind.

00:22:14.195 --> 00:22:16.107
'Cause that fear
generally is in your mind.

00:22:16.107 --> 00:22:16.940
- Yeah.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.967
- That you know, when you
get up on stage to do public

00:22:18.967 --> 00:22:22.641
speaking people are not going
to throw tomatoes at you

00:22:22.641 --> 00:22:25.245
and say oh my, you're an
idiot, get off the stage.

00:22:25.245 --> 00:22:27.347
No, they're going to sit there, you know?

00:22:27.347 --> 00:22:29.448
So there's nothing to fear.

00:22:29.448 --> 00:22:30.690
It's in your head.

00:22:30.690 --> 00:22:32.893
- [Jason] He's a large man.

00:22:32.893 --> 00:22:34.894
- You're a small man.

00:22:34.894 --> 00:22:36.111
(Jason laughs and mumbles)

00:22:36.111 --> 00:22:37.028
Yeah, yeah.

00:22:38.905 --> 00:22:41.108
- I tweeted at Jocko and I
asked him if you'd like to take

00:22:41.108 --> 00:22:43.263
part in a fitness challenge.

00:22:43.263 --> 00:22:46.537
He graciously came with a counter offer.

00:22:46.537 --> 00:22:49.502
He said, how about a grappling match?

00:22:49.502 --> 00:22:52.441
For some reason I said yes.

00:22:52.441 --> 00:22:55.197
And so here I am now in San Diego.

00:22:55.197 --> 00:22:58.030
(energetic music)

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:01.161
- [Camera Man] You're on top of 'em.

00:23:01.161 --> 00:23:02.540
Push your form--

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:04.790
(grunting)

00:23:08.098 --> 00:23:10.027
- He wants my head, he wants my head!

00:23:10.027 --> 00:23:12.258
(Jason laughs and grunts)

00:23:12.258 --> 00:23:16.425
(Jason breathing heavily and choking)

00:23:20.903 --> 00:23:23.403
(Jason yells)

00:23:30.244 --> 00:23:32.661
(bell dings)

00:23:39.959 --> 00:23:42.792
- [Camera Man] You okay? You okay?

00:23:44.903 --> 00:23:48.061
- He actually asked to get
choked out, so there it is.

00:23:48.061 --> 00:23:48.894
Ju jitsu.

00:23:55.515 --> 00:23:57.858
Fairly decisive victory,
but yeah, ya know,

00:23:57.858 --> 00:24:00.592
really, honestly, it's just
'cause I've been training

00:24:00.592 --> 00:24:02.641
for a long time, and
I have that skill set.

00:24:02.641 --> 00:24:04.483
It's something that anybody could get.

00:24:04.483 --> 00:24:05.969
It's not because I'm special.

00:24:05.969 --> 00:24:08.176
It's just 'cause I trained
for a long time doing this.

00:24:08.176 --> 00:24:10.510
And if the roles were reversed

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.042
and he'd been training longer than me,

00:24:12.042 --> 00:24:13.269
he'd be doing that right there to me.

00:24:13.269 --> 00:24:14.273
That's the way it works.

00:24:14.273 --> 00:24:15.610
- Even if I look like this
and you look like that?

00:24:15.610 --> 00:24:18.601
- Yeah, I'm more than happy
to get a 135 pounder in here

00:24:18.601 --> 00:24:19.693
right now that'll--

00:24:19.693 --> 00:24:20.776
- Show me what it's about?

00:24:20.776 --> 00:24:22.240
- They'll do you worse
than I just did you.

00:24:22.240 --> 00:24:23.497
- [Jason] I hear you.

00:24:23.497 --> 00:24:24.477
- Do you want that?

00:24:24.477 --> 00:24:25.310
- [Jason] No, I do not.

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:26.555
- I got guys that're
standing by that are hungry.

00:24:26.555 --> 00:24:28.678
- I've had enough of Jocko for one day.

00:24:28.678 --> 00:24:30.845
I don't need anybody else.

00:24:31.749 --> 00:24:33.498
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:24:33.498 --> 00:24:34.331
I hope you enjoyed

00:24:34.331 --> 00:24:37.634
I made this video because
Michael Angelo Rayco asked me to.

00:24:37.634 --> 00:24:39.299
So if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:24:39.299 --> 00:24:41.653
to profile next, leave it
down in the comments below,

00:24:41.653 --> 00:24:42.876
and I'll see what I can do.

00:24:42.876 --> 00:24:44.250
I'd also love to know, what did Jocko say

00:24:44.250 --> 00:24:46.194
that had the biggest impact of you?

00:24:46.194 --> 00:24:47.658
What clip did you enjoy the most?

00:24:47.658 --> 00:24:49.936
And what immediate action
are you going to take

00:24:49.936 --> 00:24:52.481
in your life or your business
after watching this clip?

00:24:52.481 --> 00:24:54.072
Leave it down in the comments below

00:24:54.072 --> 00:24:55.465
and I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:24:55.465 --> 00:24:57.543
Finally, I wanted to give
a quick shout out to Zeno.

00:24:57.543 --> 00:24:59.358
Thank you Zeno so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:24:59.358 --> 00:25:02.211
Your One Word and posting
that picture online.

00:25:02.211 --> 00:25:03.568
I really appreciate it.

00:25:03.568 --> 00:25:05.756
Also Zeno, thank you so
much for all the love

00:25:05.756 --> 00:25:07.853
you've given to the
Believe Nation community

00:25:07.853 --> 00:25:10.067
for being a part of almost
all of our live chats,

00:25:10.067 --> 00:25:12.471
and just being a force
for good in the comments.

00:25:12.471 --> 00:25:14.365
I really really really
appreciate your support.

00:25:14.365 --> 00:25:16.215
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:25:16.215 --> 00:25:18.283
I believe in your, I hope
you continue to believe

00:25:18.283 --> 00:25:21.205
in yourself and whatever your one word is,

00:25:21.205 --> 00:25:23.622
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:25:29.601 --> 00:25:32.101
- Nobody likes being evaluated, right?

00:25:32.101 --> 00:25:32.934
Nobody.

00:25:34.198 --> 00:25:35.861
Now, you might get somebody that says

00:25:35.861 --> 00:25:37.253
oh, I love being coached.

00:25:37.253 --> 00:25:38.925
And there are some people
that are pretty positive

00:25:38.925 --> 00:25:40.881
about that, and as matter
of fact I have clients

00:25:40.881 --> 00:25:44.350
where they want to be coached, right?

00:25:44.350 --> 00:25:46.933
But most people, especially
in a normal environment

00:25:46.933 --> 00:25:48.706
like if you go out and you
hire someone to coach you,

00:25:48.706 --> 00:25:49.539
okay.

00:25:51.198 --> 00:25:55.080
But most people in a normal
environment, they don't like

00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:56.796
being evaluated.

00:25:56.796 --> 00:26:00.546
They don't like being
judged, always judging.

00:26:02.409 --> 00:26:05.196
So, the first thing you have
to do when it comes to being

00:26:05.196 --> 00:26:09.155
evaluated is get that
in your head that you,

00:26:09.155 --> 00:26:11.798
like everybody else
has defense mechanisms.

00:26:11.798 --> 00:26:16.259
And they're going to flair
up as soon as somebody says

00:26:16.259 --> 00:26:17.984
something critical of you.

00:26:17.984 --> 00:26:20.487
As soon as somebody goes to evaluate you.

00:26:20.487 --> 00:26:22.713
Your defense mechanisms
are going to go up.

00:26:22.713 --> 00:26:24.302
And then once that happens,

00:26:24.302 --> 00:26:26.551
once you feel those
defense mechanisms go up,

00:26:26.551 --> 00:26:29.218
you got to put your ego in check.

00:26:31.465 --> 00:26:34.928
You got to put your ego in check.

00:26:34.928 --> 00:26:38.411
And then once you do
that, you got to listen.

00:26:38.411 --> 00:26:41.400
Listen, I know it sounds
crazy, listen to what

00:26:41.400 --> 00:26:42.796
they're saying.

00:26:42.796 --> 00:26:45.379
Don't even think of a response.

00:26:46.339 --> 00:26:48.239
Say to yourself, you know
what, I'm not even going to

00:26:48.239 --> 00:26:51.728
respond, I'm only going to
listen to what they're saying.

00:26:51.728 --> 00:26:53.641
- Yeah, but, and to kind of add to that--

00:26:53.641 --> 00:26:55.190
- Dude, you're already can't even take it.

00:26:55.190 --> 00:26:56.221
- No, no, I can take it.

00:26:56.221 --> 00:26:57.054
- Oh, okay.

00:26:57.054 --> 00:26:58.960
- I'm saying but I
think, 'cause people will

00:26:58.960 --> 00:27:01.622
quote, unquote do that, but
they won't really do it,

00:27:01.622 --> 00:27:03.382
as far as I'm not going to say anything,

00:27:03.382 --> 00:27:04.757
I'm just going to listen.

00:27:04.757 --> 00:27:06.403
- Yeah, that's actually, that's actually,

00:27:06.403 --> 00:27:08.283
that's actually how they set it up too,

00:27:08.283 --> 00:27:10.147
look, I'm not going to say
anything, I'm just going to listen.

00:27:10.147 --> 00:27:11.391
- Yeah, exactly what I'm talking about.

00:27:11.391 --> 00:27:13.006
(begins and cuts off many words)

00:27:13.006 --> 00:27:14.769
Or they'll all body language,

00:27:14.769 --> 00:27:17.081
you know the kind where they're like.

00:27:17.081 --> 00:27:19.377
You know, they'll do that kind of stuff.

00:27:19.377 --> 00:27:21.483
Don't do that, don't do that.

00:27:21.483 --> 00:27:22.985
- So you're right, you got to listen,

00:27:22.985 --> 00:27:24.937
and not just listen, but truly listen.

00:27:24.937 --> 00:27:26.598
Not listening just with your ears,

00:27:26.598 --> 00:27:28.343
but listen with your mind and your brain

00:27:28.343 --> 00:27:30.985
and with an open mind.

00:27:30.985 --> 00:27:32.746
An open mind.

00:27:32.746 --> 00:27:34.959
And then think about
what people are saying.

00:27:34.959 --> 00:27:36.938
And then see it, this is important,

00:27:36.938 --> 00:27:38.602
see it from their perspective.

00:27:38.602 --> 00:27:40.600
Because if you just see
it from your perspective,

00:27:40.600 --> 00:27:42.870
you're not even seeing what
the criticism really is.

00:27:42.870 --> 00:27:46.918
You're only seeing the
defense of the criticism.

00:27:46.918 --> 00:27:49.215
So actually get in their mind

00:27:49.215 --> 00:27:51.204
and say wow, what does this look like

00:27:51.204 --> 00:27:52.907
from their perspective?

00:27:52.907 --> 00:27:55.234
Why would they be taking the effort

00:27:55.234 --> 00:27:58.674
and the risk and the
challenge of trying to present

00:27:58.674 --> 00:28:01.612
this problem to me if it wasn't important?

00:28:01.612 --> 00:28:04.156
Are they just doing it
just to make me mad?

00:28:04.156 --> 00:28:05.139
No.

00:28:05.139 --> 00:28:06.227
They're trying to help you.

00:28:06.227 --> 00:28:07.637
And you know what?

00:28:07.637 --> 00:28:10.354
Just like, just like a
joke, ya know how they say

00:28:10.354 --> 00:28:14.147
like every joke has
some little truth to it?

00:28:14.147 --> 00:28:17.171
Every little criticism,
even if the person is your

00:28:17.171 --> 00:28:21.338
arch rival, their criticism
is built on something.

00:28:24.122 --> 00:28:28.494
So what is that reality that
you can take away from it.

00:28:28.494 --> 00:28:30.143
You got to take it with a grain of salt,

00:28:30.143 --> 00:28:31.727
especially if the person,
like it says here,

00:28:31.727 --> 00:28:33.667
if the person has different
opinions and motives,

00:28:33.667 --> 00:28:35.522
well of course they
have different opinions.

00:28:35.522 --> 00:28:37.376
You want people with different opinions.

00:28:37.376 --> 00:28:39.182
Maybe they have different
motives, so maybe you think

00:28:39.182 --> 00:28:41.353
they're trying to usurp your authority

00:28:41.353 --> 00:28:43.045
or something like that.

00:28:43.045 --> 00:28:47.663
So, maybe you got to take
it with a grain of salt,

00:28:47.663 --> 00:28:50.871
but find the grain of truth in there too.

00:28:50.871 --> 00:28:53.902
And find what it is
from their perspective,

00:28:53.902 --> 00:28:57.152
what the problem is, and learn from it.

00:28:58.017 --> 00:29:00.058
And one of the most beautiful
things about this is,

00:29:00.058 --> 00:29:04.058
you take the criticism
and you make adjustments.

00:29:04.989 --> 00:29:07.289
You know, how do I deal
with being evaluated?

00:29:07.289 --> 00:29:10.693
I try and accept the
evaluation and make adjustments

00:29:10.693 --> 00:29:13.110
to improve myself as a human.

00:29:15.048 --> 00:29:18.016
That's how I deal with being evaluated.

00:29:18.016 --> 00:29:20.080
And I'm not saying I
deal with it any better

00:29:20.080 --> 00:29:21.402
than anybody else.

00:29:21.402 --> 00:29:26.085
Because everybody gets
defensive, myself included.

00:29:26.085 --> 00:29:27.981
You know, we had a little conversation

00:29:27.981 --> 00:29:30.230
when we started tonight, right?

00:29:30.230 --> 00:29:31.248
- [Interviewer] Sure.

00:29:31.248 --> 00:29:34.865
- You said I repeated some
stuff on the last podcast.

00:29:34.865 --> 00:29:36.101
- [Interviewer] Allegedly.

00:29:36.101 --> 00:29:39.848
- And you know, and then
we talked through it,

00:29:39.848 --> 00:29:43.012
and then I said, you know,
and you know, I noticed

00:29:43.012 --> 00:29:44.913
that your camera work
was a little bit off.

00:29:44.913 --> 00:29:45.746
(laughter)

00:29:45.746 --> 00:29:46.746
Ya know it was just,

00:29:46.746 --> 00:29:49.750
My point was just to prove
how defensive we all get.

00:29:49.750 --> 00:29:50.583
We all get.

00:29:50.583 --> 00:29:51.541
And you know what I did?

00:29:51.541 --> 00:29:52.665
I said, you know what?

00:29:52.665 --> 00:29:54.970
I noticed that too, ya know,
as far as me repeating,

00:29:54.970 --> 00:29:56.859
there was a couple little sections

00:29:56.859 --> 00:29:59.246
and it was because, I pulled
from multiple different

00:29:59.246 --> 00:30:01.960
books and they had a
little bit of overlap.

00:30:01.960 --> 00:30:03.947
- [Interviewer] Yep, saying the same, yep.

00:30:03.947 --> 00:30:06.869
- And looking back on it,
probably shouldn't have,

00:30:06.869 --> 00:30:08.847
but at the time I thought you know what,

00:30:08.847 --> 00:30:11.975
this is emphasizing
really important points.

00:30:11.975 --> 00:30:12.808
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:30:12.808 --> 00:30:13.891
- But still.

00:30:13.891 --> 00:30:15.542
People don't want to hear the
same thing over and over again.

00:30:15.542 --> 00:30:17.149
So I probably shouldn't have done that.

00:30:17.149 --> 00:30:20.066
So, guess what, criticism accepted.

00:30:20.958 --> 00:30:24.315
I will adapt, adjust and
I will make improvements

00:30:24.315 --> 00:30:26.805
to my game based on your
criticism of my technique,

00:30:26.805 --> 00:30:29.195
my skill and my life.

00:30:29.195 --> 00:30:32.154
There's so much knowledge out there,

00:30:32.154 --> 00:30:36.154
so much information, so
many ways to get better.

00:30:38.409 --> 00:30:41.576
And we make, we make so many mistakes.

00:30:44.587 --> 00:30:47.420
We're the product of our mistakes.

00:30:48.579 --> 00:30:52.162
And often times the
lesson is sitting there

00:30:53.337 --> 00:30:55.651
right in front of our face.

00:30:55.651 --> 00:30:57.536
It's there to be learned, but we miss it

00:30:57.536 --> 00:30:59.041
or we don't pay attention to it

00:30:59.041 --> 00:31:01.291
or we think we know better.

00:31:03.373 --> 00:31:06.040
Until it punches us in the face.

00:31:11.281 --> 00:31:14.450
And the most important
thing to learn is that

00:31:14.450 --> 00:31:16.533
we have so much to learn,

00:31:17.566 --> 00:31:19.007
we all do.

00:31:19.007 --> 00:31:22.743
And we can learn from
school and from people

00:31:22.743 --> 00:31:26.326
and from experience
and we learn from life.

00:31:30.375 --> 00:31:34.179
But ya have to process the information,

00:31:34.179 --> 00:31:37.779
you have to absorb it,
ya have to accept it.

00:31:37.779 --> 00:31:40.361
Ya have to open your mind.

00:31:40.361 --> 00:31:42.864
You've got to free your mind.

00:31:42.864 --> 00:31:44.697
So that you can learn.

00:31:45.985 --> 00:31:47.902
And make real progress.

00:31:54.524 --> 00:31:57.941
And as far as regrets and things I wish I

00:31:59.174 --> 00:32:03.007
would have done differently,
of course, hindsight,

00:32:05.465 --> 00:32:08.960
hindsight is 20/20 and looking
back, who wouldn't want

00:32:08.960 --> 00:32:10.879
to take another go at something

00:32:10.879 --> 00:32:15.024
and improve on the first
try by doing it again?

00:32:15.024 --> 00:32:19.150
And then why not do it
again and again and again?

00:32:19.150 --> 00:32:22.449
And why not just do it over
and over again until you

00:32:22.449 --> 00:32:23.782
have it perfect?

00:32:28.534 --> 00:32:32.117
But the fact is, you
don't get that chance.

00:32:35.483 --> 00:32:36.900
You get one shot.

00:32:38.402 --> 00:32:41.069
One shot at this gig right here.

00:32:42.550 --> 00:32:44.008
Life.

00:32:44.008 --> 00:32:46.675
One life, that's all you've got.

00:32:48.216 --> 00:32:50.633
And regret, in and of itself,

00:32:54.546 --> 00:32:56.475
it's worthless.

00:32:56.475 --> 00:32:58.519
It does nothing for you.

00:32:58.519 --> 00:33:02.060
In fact, the only valuable thing in regret

00:33:02.060 --> 00:33:04.227
is the lesson you learned.

00:33:05.921 --> 00:33:08.421
The knowledge that you gained.

00:33:10.209 --> 00:33:14.376
But walking around filled
with regret gets you nothing.

00:33:18.470 --> 00:33:20.303
So, learn and move on.

00:33:22.575 --> 00:33:25.189
Don't let regret beat you down.

00:33:25.189 --> 00:33:27.716
Don't be a slave to regret.

00:33:27.716 --> 00:33:28.549
No.

00:33:29.567 --> 00:33:32.984
Let it teach you, let it make you better.

00:33:36.022 --> 00:33:39.855
Let the fear of regret
fuel you to take action

00:33:41.213 --> 00:33:42.130
today, now.

00:33:46.218 --> 00:33:49.968
To take action now to
become a better person,

00:33:52.575 --> 00:33:54.492
not filled with regret,

00:33:57.028 --> 00:33:59.195
but filled with knowledge.

00:34:03.405 --> 00:34:07.689
Filled with knowledge
and strength and power

00:34:07.689 --> 00:34:09.439
and filled with life.

00:34:12.200 --> 00:34:14.148
With the man in the cave

00:34:14.148 --> 00:34:17.815
and this idea and this
thought of the enemy.

00:34:20.247 --> 00:34:23.808
And that was a thought
that used to drive me.

00:34:23.808 --> 00:34:27.995
And kind of haunt me
and make me get up early

00:34:27.995 --> 00:34:31.011
and work hard to push myself.

00:34:31.011 --> 00:34:34.344
Because I knew that somewhere out there,

00:34:38.516 --> 00:34:40.804
there was an enemy, a real enemy,

00:34:40.804 --> 00:34:43.221
a real man, a person, a human

00:34:46.870 --> 00:34:48.495
that was waiting for me,

00:34:48.495 --> 00:34:50.708
that was preparing for me.

00:34:50.708 --> 00:34:52.541
And therefore I needed

00:34:56.133 --> 00:34:58.382
to prepare for him.

00:34:58.382 --> 00:34:59.834
I needed to be ready.

00:34:59.834 --> 00:35:02.147
I needed to be the things
I always talk about.

00:35:02.147 --> 00:35:04.805
I needed to be stronger,
and faster and smarter

00:35:04.805 --> 00:35:05.722
and better.

00:35:07.824 --> 00:35:11.407
So that when we did
meet on the battlefield

00:35:15.499 --> 00:35:20.436
I would be ready for that
rendezvous, for that meeting,

00:35:20.436 --> 00:35:21.269
that fate.

00:35:23.705 --> 00:35:24.705
That battle.

00:35:26.874 --> 00:35:30.243
And that thought, that
thought of the enemy, yes,

00:35:30.243 --> 00:35:32.243
it absolutely fueled me.

00:35:36.286 --> 00:35:39.004
And when I was a leader in the SEAL teams,

00:35:39.004 --> 00:35:42.587
in charge of men, it
was even more profound

00:35:45.695 --> 00:35:50.038
because I was thinking
about that rendezvous.

00:35:50.038 --> 00:35:53.088
For everybody that I led,
everyone I was in charge of,

00:35:53.088 --> 00:35:55.088
everyone that I trained.

00:35:57.446 --> 00:36:01.613
And I felt that burden, the
burden of responsibility.

00:36:03.479 --> 00:36:07.118
To prepare those men, and protect those,

00:36:07.118 --> 00:36:10.618
those men, those frog men, those warriors.

00:36:15.510 --> 00:36:16.510
My brothers.

00:36:21.740 --> 00:36:25.907
And it was my burden to train
those guys and prepare them.

00:36:33.033 --> 00:36:37.743
And that burden, it may have
made me a little bit crazy,

00:36:37.743 --> 00:36:41.743
a little be paranoid, a
little bit over the top.

00:36:46.176 --> 00:36:48.676
But, I didn't really know any,

00:36:52.423 --> 00:36:53.590
any other way.

00:37:01.389 --> 00:37:02.306
And so now,

00:37:07.089 --> 00:37:08.256
I am no longer

00:37:12.237 --> 00:37:13.570
a combat leader.

00:37:16.155 --> 00:37:18.822
I no longer prepare men for war.

00:37:22.536 --> 00:37:23.536
So the drive

00:37:25.839 --> 00:37:27.339
and the motivation

00:37:29.287 --> 00:37:31.454
is from a different place.

00:37:35.933 --> 00:37:38.016
It's from a solemn place.

00:37:41.763 --> 00:37:44.583
The drive now and the motivation now

00:37:44.583 --> 00:37:47.666
is not really from the enemy anymore.

00:37:54.142 --> 00:37:57.309
Now it's from my friends, my brothers.

00:38:01.043 --> 00:38:03.793
It's from those SEALs that I knew

00:38:18.282 --> 00:38:19.115
and that I

00:38:25.240 --> 00:38:27.823
cared about more than anything.

00:38:31.767 --> 00:38:33.767
And that they sacrificed

00:38:37.975 --> 00:38:38.808
everything

00:38:43.225 --> 00:38:44.475
for us, for me.

00:38:46.196 --> 00:38:49.613
Those guys, they gave their lives for us.

00:39:01.867 --> 00:39:02.700
And now

00:39:04.428 --> 00:39:08.595
I cannot help but think and
remember that every breath

00:39:11.977 --> 00:39:13.394
that we take is a

00:39:17.149 --> 00:39:18.559
it's a gift.

00:39:18.559 --> 00:39:21.392
It's a sacred gift from those men.

00:39:24.784 --> 00:39:28.623
Every day we have, every
sunrise, every thought

00:39:28.623 --> 00:39:31.201
and every smile and every laugh,

00:39:31.201 --> 00:39:32.201
it's a gift.

00:39:39.823 --> 00:39:42.323
And I will treasure that gift,

00:39:45.347 --> 00:39:46.847
that gift of life.

00:39:51.094 --> 00:39:55.261
And I will not let it go to
waste, not one second of it.

00:39:59.580 --> 00:40:03.065
And I'll cherish every moment of it.

00:40:03.065 --> 00:40:04.648
And I will live it.

00:40:06.592 --> 00:40:07.842
I will live it.

00:40:11.715 --> 00:40:13.048
In their memory.

00:40:17.686 --> 00:40:19.353
And in their honor.

